.TH CLAY 1 "August 2026" "clay 0.0.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clay \- focused AI coding agent for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clay
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B clay shell
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clay
connects to OpenAI, OpenAI Codex, Grok, OpenRouter, Groq, DeepSeek, Mistral,
Together AI, or another OpenAI-compatible endpoint and provides a terminal
coding workflow with file tools, checkpoints, memory, and streaming responses.
.PP
Run without a prompt for the interactive interface. Use
.B --prompt
for a single non-interactive request.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable terminal colors.
.TP
.BI --cwd= directory
Change to DIRECTORY before starting.
.TP
.BI --prompt= text
Send TEXT and exit after one response.
.TP
.BI -p\  text
Short alias for
.BR --prompt .
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B /connect
Connect a provider. Use
.B /connect openai-codex
for ChatGPT Plus/Pro OAuth, or select a named OpenAI-compatible provider.
.TP
.B /model
Choose or set the active model.
.TP
.B /undo
Undo the most recent successful
.B write
or
.B edit
without restoring the entire workspace. Undo is kept for the current session
and refuses to overwrite a file that changed afterwards.
.TP
.B /checkpoints
List and restore whole-workspace checkpoints.
.TP
.B /tasks
List running background commands and select one to stop.
.TP
.B /resume
Resume a saved conversation.
.TP
.B /help
List all interactive commands.
.TP
.B /exit
Quit clay.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLAY_PROVIDER, CLAY_MODEL
Select a provider and model explicitly.
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, GROQ_API_KEY
API keys for the corresponding providers.
.TP
.B DEEPSEEK_API_KEY, MISTRAL_API_KEY, TOGETHER_API_KEY
API keys for the corresponding OpenAI-compatible providers.
.TP
.B CLAY_API_KEY, CLAY_BASE_URL, CUSTOM_MODEL
Credentials and endpoint for the custom provider.
.PP
Provider-specific base URLs and model variables are documented in the project
README.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.clay/
Configuration, credentials, chat journals, checkpoints, and memory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR curl (1)
